  "seoBody": "<div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>Farm machinery is governed by PUWER 1998; lifting equipment such as telehandlers and loaders also falls under LOLER 1998</li><li>The Safe Stop principle is the core discipline: handbrake on, controls in neutral, engine off, key out</li><li>Guarding, especially of PTO shafts, is critical because being caught in moving machinery is a repeat killer</li><li>A pre-use walk-round check is good practice; the value is in it happening at the machine and being recorded</li><li>The checklist does not maintain the machine. Competent maintenance does. The record is the evidence it was checked</li></ul></div><h2>Why the machinery check matters on a farm</h2><p>Moving machinery is one of the repeat killers on British farms in the HSE figures, and unguarded parts and power take-off (PTO) shafts appear year after year. A pre-use check on a tractor or an implement is not complicated, but it only counts if it actually happens at the machine and if there is a record to prove it. The checklist does not maintain the machine. Competent maintenance and a competent operator do. The record is the evidence the check was carried out.</p><h2>PUWER, LOLER and the law</h2><p>The Provision and Use of Work Equipment Regulations 1998 (PUWER) require work equipment to be suitable, maintained in a safe condition, inspected where needed, and used only by trained people. A tractor, baler, mower and mixer wagon all sit under PUWER. Where a machine lifts, such as a telehandler or a front loader, the Lifting Operations and Lifting Equipment Regulations 1998 (LOLER) add a duty of thorough examination at set intervals. None of this prescribes a specific checklist. This page is a guide, not legal advice; check the current HSE and PUWER guidance for your machines.</p><h2>A pre-use tractor check, item by item</h2><p>A daily or pre-use check typically covers the following. Adapt it to the machine and the manufacturer's handbook.</p><ul><li><strong>Guards</strong> - all fitted and intact, PTO shaft guard present and free to rotate</li><li><strong>Brakes</strong> - service and parking brakes hold; brake pedals latched for road work</li><li><strong>Steering</strong> - responsive, no excessive play</li><li><strong>Tyres</strong> - condition, tread, pressure, no visible damage</li><li><strong>Lights and beacon</strong> - side, rear, indicators, work lights and rotating beacon all working</li><li><strong>Mirrors and glass</strong> - clean, secure, clear view</li><li><strong>Fluids</strong> - oil, coolant, hydraulic and fuel levels, no visible leaks</li><li><strong>Cab</strong> - ROPS and seatbelt present and used</li><li><strong>Hitching</strong> - linkage, pins and PTO connection secure before work</li></ul><h2>Safe Stop</h2><p>Safe Stop is the single most important habit on a farm machine, and the HSE promotes it directly. Before anyone leaves the seat, gets off, or approaches a moving part: handbrake on, controls in neutral, engine off, key out. People are still killed because a machine was left running or in gear while someone cleared a blockage or checked a hitch. A checklist can prompt Safe Stop, but it cannot enforce it. That is the operator's discipline; the record captures that the machine was left safe.</p><h2>What to look for in a machinery check tool</h2><ul><li><strong>On-site completion:</strong> the operator completes the walk-round at the machine, not later from memory</li><li><strong>Photo of the fault:</strong> a defect captured as a dated image, not a note that gets lost</li><li><strong>Works with gloves and no signal:</strong> a word, a voice note or a photo, not a form that needs full bars</li><li><strong>No per-seat penalty:</strong> per-seat pricing charges for every operator and relief driver who never files. Quickler is £20 per active user per month, dormant users free, everything unlimited</li><li><strong>Evidence trail:</strong> date, operator, machine, every item and any fault, for the HSE, an insurer or an assurance assessor</li></ul><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Honest note:</strong> Quickler captures the check and generates the record. It does not maintain the machine, replace a competent fitter, or stand in for an NPTC certificate of competence where one is needed. It records what the operator checked, with a date and a photo. The safe machine comes from the maintenance and the operator. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> if that distinction matters for your farm.</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What should a farm machinery inspection checklist include?</h3><p>A pre-use tractor check usually covers guards and the PTO shaft guard, service and parking brakes, steering, tyres, lights and beacon, mirrors and glass, fluid levels and leaks, the ROPS and seatbelt, and secure hitching. Adapt it to the specific machine and the manufacturer's handbook. The value is in the check happening at the machine and being recorded.</p><h3>Is a daily tractor check a legal requirement?</h3><p>PUWER 1998 requires work equipment to be maintained in a safe condition and used by trained people, and inspected where needed. It does not mandate a specific daily form, but a pre-use check is widely expected good practice and gives you the record to show the machine was fit. Check the current HSE and PUWER guidance for your situation.</p><h3>What is the Safe Stop principle?</h3><p>Safe Stop is the discipline of making a farm machine safe before anyone leaves the seat or approaches moving parts: handbrake on, controls in neutral, engine off, key out. The HSE promotes it because leaving a machine running or in gear is a repeat cause of serious injury and death on farms.</p><h3>Can I record a machinery check over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's machinery check runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The operator receives each item in their existing WhatsApp chat, answers with a word, a voice note or a photo of a fault, and the completed record generates automatically with a date and image. No separate app or login is required, and Quickler manages the WhatsApp Business API account on the farm's behalf.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/farm-safety-inspection-app-uk.html\">Farm safety inspection app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/farm-risk-assessment-app-uk.html\">Farm risk assessment app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/red-tractor-assurance-records-uk.html\">Red Tractor assurance records</a></li></ul>",
